OTP_Provisioner station gadget: rpi-fastbootd that cannot read the board back

Applied by docker/gadget.Dockerfile to rpi-fastbootd cca05b29f3ce1276151973398867b5c82c38ae40, the
revision pi-gen-micro vendors (internal/packages/rpi-fastbootd_14.0.0~git20260902.cca05b2_arm64.deb).
The signed gadget a board boots from the station is driven by whoever runs the provisioning page, so
the daemon in it only does what that page needs:

* commands: download, upload, getvar (without private-key), shutdown, reboot, erase, flash, oem;
* shutdown powers the board off (systemctl poweroff; upstream only paused the daemon): the station ends
  stage 3 with it, so the first boot of the new system does not run on the station's USB power;
* oem: idpinit/idpwrite/idpgetblk/idpdone, fwcrypto init, the new cryptcheck, and upload-file /
  download-file for the otp-keyexport helper's files only (/run/otp-keyexport/{key.der,status,request});
  cryptopen, mount, partinit/partapp, cryptinit/cryptsetpassword, verity*, gpioset, led, bmap-*,
  eeprom-* and the other fwcrypto operations are refused;
* oem cryptcheck <blkdev>: checks that the LUKS key the board derives from OTP opens the container
  (crypt_activate_by_passphrase without a name), so no decrypted device is ever created;
* USB only: "-i usb+tcp" from run_fastboot is ignored (the TCP data plane flashes and erases);
* debian/gen-version.sh: OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX puts the build above the upstream version.

diff --git a/debian/gen-version.sh b/debian/gen-version.sh
index 9b1632b..cf0f993 100755
--- a/debian/gen-version.sh
+++ b/debian/gen-version.sh
@@ -29,6 +29,20 @@ echo "Generating debian/changelog with version ${VERSION}..."
 # Start fresh changelog
 > "${OUTPUT}"
 
+# OTP_Provisioner: a patched build is versioned above the upstream revision it is built from
+# (OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX, e.g. "+otp1"), so apt prefers it and dpkg says what it is.
+if [ -n "${OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX:-}" ]; then
+    case "${OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX}" in *[!A-Za-z0-9.+~]*) echo "bad OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
+    cat >> "${OUTPUT}" << EOF
+${PACKAGE_NAME} (${VERSION}${OTP_FASTBOOTD_SUFFIX}) ${DISTRIBUTION}; urgency=medium
+
+  * OTP_Provisioner station gadget: command allowlist, oem cryptcheck, USB only.
+
+ -- OTP_Provisioner <otp-provisioner@localhost>  $(git show -s --format=%aD HEAD)
+
+EOF
+fi
+
 # Get all commits after baseline (newest first for Debian changelog format)
 mapfile -t COMMITS < <(git rev-list ${BASELINE_COMMIT}^..HEAD 2>/dev/null || true)
 
